      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When challenged, do not engage in a defensive argument about your origins; instead, calmly redirect the focus back to the present issue at hand. A simple, unwavering acknowledgement like, \"My perspective is informed by a scope of experience that goes beyond this discussion, but I understand your concern about [topic],\" can firmly close the door on further questioning. Maintain direct eye contact and maintain your composed posture, allowing your bearing—not your words—to communicate the unassailability of your insight.",
